  "result": "Here's what I found: the site builds its timetable from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warning code yet. So the first question is where the site would learn that a sailing is cancelled.\n\nThat matters because a nightly file can only carry cancellations decided the day before. Many cancellations happen on the day, because of weather or a breakdown. If those are the ones you care about, the site needs a faster way to hear about them, and that shapes most of what gets built.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that decision get made and passed on, and who knows about it first?",
